 wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For cutting ingredients</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-3416-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-3416-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"3416\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Instructions</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3416-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 1: Heat the Oil &#8211; Heat oil in a large pot over medium heat. Let it warm up nicely.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3416-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 2: Sauté Onion and Garlic &#8211; Add onion and garlic; sauté until translucent. The aroma will be delightful!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3416-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 3: Brown the Chicken &#8211; Add chicken pieces and brown on all sides. This adds a lovely flavor.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3416-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 4: Add the Flavor &#8211; Stir in tomato sauce, bell pepper, oregano, cumin, salt, and pepper. Mix it all together!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3416-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 5: Pour in Chicken Broth &#8211; Pour in chicken broth and bring to a boil. Let those flavors mingle!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3416-step-0-5\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 6: Add Vegetables &#8211; Add potatoes and carrot, reduce heat, cover, and simmer for 25–30 minutes until vegetables and chicken are tender.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3416-step-0-6\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 7: Garnish and Serve &#8211; Garnish with fresh cilantro and serve hot. Enjoy your delicious pollo guisado!</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-3416-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrition Facts</th>\n<th>Per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>350</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>15g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>30g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>25g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Gather these simple ingredients to create a delicious pollo guisado that will impress your family and friends!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Ingredients-for-Pollo-Guisado.webp\" alt=\"A vibrant display of ingredients for pollo guisado on a wooden kitchen table, featuring chicken, vegetables, and spices.\" class=\"wp-image-3414\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Ingredients-for-Pollo-Guisado.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Ingredients-for-Pollo-Guisado-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>1 kg chicken pieces</strong> – your choice of chicken cuts</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 tbsp vegetable oil</strong> – for cooking</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 onion</strong> – chopped</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>3 garlic cloves</strong> – minced</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1/4 cup tomato sauce</strong> – adds richness</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 bell pepper</strong> – chopped</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 potatoes</strong> – peeled and chopped</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 carrot</strong> – sliced</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 tsp dried oregano</strong> – for flavor</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 tsp ground </strong><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cumin\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>cumin</strong> </a>– adds warmth</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 cup chicken broth</strong> – for depth of flavor</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Salt and pepper</strong> – to taste</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Fresh cilantro</strong> – for garnish</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-pollo-guisado\"><strong>How to Make Pollo Guisado</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready to enjoy a delicious homemade pollo guisado! This comforting dish takes about 15 minutes to prepare and 30 minutes to cook, making it perfect for a cozy dinner. Let’s dive into the steps!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Step-by-Step-Pollo-Guisado-Preparation.webp\" alt=\"A step-by-step visual representation of making pollo guisado, showcasing heating oil, sautéing onions and garlic, browning chicken, and mixing in spices.\" class=\"wp-image-3415\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Step-by-Step-Pollo-Guisado-Preparation.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Step-by-Step-Pollo-Guisado-Preparation-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Heat the Oil</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Heat oil in a large pot over medium heat. Let it warm up nicely.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Sauté Onion and Garlic</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Add onion and garlic; sauté until translucent. The aroma will be delightful!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Brown the Chicken</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Add chicken pieces and brown on all sides. This adds a lovely flavor.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Add the Flavor</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Stir in tomato sauce, bell pepper, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oregano\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">oregano</a>, cumin, salt, and pepper. Mix it all together!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Pour in Chicken Broth</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Pour in chicken broth and bring to a boil. Let those flavors mingle!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 6: Add Vegetables</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Add potatoes and carrot, reduce heat, cover, and simmer for 25–30 minutes until vegetables and chicken are tender.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 7: Garnish and Serve</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Garnish with fresh cilantro and serve hot. Enjoy your delicious pollo guisado!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Main Course</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>Latin American</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>15 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>30 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>0 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>45 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Not specified</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Hot with fresh cilantro garnish!</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-pollo-guisado\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making pollo guisado</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Marinate the chicken overnight for deeper flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use fresh herbs like cilantro for a vibrant finish.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Opt for low-sodium chicken broth to control saltiness.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Let it simmer longer for tender, juicy chicken.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve with warm tortillas for a comforting touch.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-pollo-guisado\"><strong>How to Serve this pollo guisado</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Serve with fluffy white rice to soak up the delicious sauce.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with warm tortillas for a delightful wrap.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add a side of black beans for extra protein and flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Top with fresh avocado slices for a creamy contrast.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Garnish with chopped cilantro and lime wedges for a zesty kick.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Enjoy with a refreshing cucumber salad to balance the richness.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Storing and enjoying your pollo guisado later is easy!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Let the pollo guisado cool to room temperature.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Transfer to an airtight container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store in the refrigerator for up to 3 days.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label the container with the date for easy tracking.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Cool the dish completely before freezing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use freezer-safe containers or heavy-duty freezer bags.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Remove as much air as possible to prevent freezer burn.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Freeze for up to 3 months for best quality.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Thaw in the refrigerator overnight before reheating.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Reheat on the stovetop over medium heat, stirring occasionally.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add a splash of chicken broth or water if it seems dry.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Ensure it reaches an internal temperature of 165°F (74°C) before serving.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \">1. <strong>What ingredients are in pollo guisado?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Pollo guisado typically includes bone-in chicken, potatoes, carrots, bell peppers, onions, garlic, and tomatoes. It&#8217;s seasoned with cumin, paprika, oregano, and a splash of apple cider vinegar for brightness. A bit of honey adds natural sweetness, and the dish is finished with fresh cilantro and scallions for a burst of flavor.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \">2. <strong>How do I thicken my pollo guisado?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>To thicken your pollo guisado, let it simmer uncovered so the liquid reduces. You can also mash a few of the potatoes or add a spoonful of tomato paste. If needed, stir in a cornstarch slurry (1 tablespoon cornstarch mixed with 2 tablespoons water) and simmer until the sauce thickens.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \">3. <strong>What does pollo guisado mean in Spanish?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p><em>Pollo guisado</em> means “stewed chicken” in Spanish. It refers to chicken that’s slow-cooked in a flavorful broth with vegetables and seasonings until tender.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \">4. <strong>Why is my pollo guisado watery?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Your pollo guisado might be watery if too much liquid was added or if it wasn’t simmered long enough. Make sure to cook it uncovered toward the end to let excess liquid evaporate. Also, avoid overloading the pot with vegetables that release lots of water, like tomatoes or zucchini.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Now that you’ve got the scoop on making delicious pollo guisado, it’s time to roll up your sleeves and dive in! This dish is not just a meal; it’s a warm hug on a plate. Enjoy the simple pleasure of cooking and savor every bite. Your kitchen will smell amazing, and your taste buds will thank you!</p>\n",
